{"task_id": "HumanEval/43", "solution": "def pairs_sum_to_zero(l):\n    \"\"\"\n    pairs_sum_to_zero takes a list of integers as an input.\n    it returns True if there are two distinct elements in the list that\n    sum to zero, and False otherwise.\n    >>> pairs_sum_to_zero([1, 3, 5, 0])\n    False\n    >>> pairs_sum_to_zero([1, 3, -2, 1])\n    False\n    >>> pairs_sum_to_zero([1, 2, 3, 7])\n    False\n    >>> pairs_sum_to_zero([2, 4, -5, 3, 5, 7])\n    True\n    >>> pairs_sum_to_zero([1])\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n    # If the list has fewer than two elements, no pair can be formed.\n    if len(l) < 2:\n        return False\n\n    # Iterate through all unique pairs of elements to check their sum.\n    for i in range(len(l)):\n        for j in range(i + 1, len(l)):\n            if l[i] + l[j] == 0:\n                return True\n    \n    # Return False if no distinct elements sum to zero.\n    return False"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/43", "solution": "def pairs_sum_to_zero(l):\n    \"\"\"\n    pairs_sum_to_zero takes a list of integers as an input.\n    it returns True if there are two distinct elements in the list that\n    sum to zero, and False otherwise.\n    >>> pairs_sum_to_zero([1, 3, 5, 0])\n    False\n    >>> pairs_sum_to_zero([1, 3, -2, 1])\n    False\n    >>> pairs_sum_to_zero([1, 2, 3, 7])\n    False\n    >>> pairs_sum_to_zero([2, 4, -5, 3, 5, 7])\n    True\n    >>> pairs_sum_to_zero([1])\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(l)\n    # If the list has fewer than 2 elements, no distinct pair can be formed.\n    if n < 2:\n        return False\n\n    # Iterate through all distinct pairs of elements by their indices.\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            # If the sum of the elements at these distinct positions is zero, return True.\n            if l[i] + l[j] == 0:\n                return True\n    \n    # If no such pair is found after checking all combinations, return False.\n    return False"}
