{"task_id": "HumanEval/151", "solution": "```python\ndef double_the_difference(lst):\n    '''\n    Calculates the sum of squares of odd positive integers from the input list.\n    Ignores negative numbers, non-integers, and even numbers.\n    '''\n    total_sum = 0\n\n    if not lst:\n        return 0\n\n    for num in lst:\n        # Validate if the number is positive and effectively an integer.\n        # This handles floats that represent integers (e.g., 5.0) and filters out non-integers (e.g., 1.5).\n        if num > 0 and num == int(num):\n            # Check if the integer part of the number is odd.\n            if int(num) % 2 != 0:\n                total_sum += int(num) * int(num)\n    return total_sum\n```"}
